A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312960} :answer-field/id #uuid "4250f857-367a-5f5f-8a93-ed84312a5c67" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a89705-7950-5955-8120-25d5c81b461c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Cx{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312631} {:answer/id #uuid "5783be6f-a8b4-59cd-82b6-c300877427ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312678} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5f02e1-7e39-54f2-a0a8-6069f70ed6a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313113} {:answer/id #uuid "dc69ceaf-36c0-5d3f-9423-23df22533d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc69ceaf-36c0-5d3f-9423-23df22533d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313711} :answer-field/id #uuid "76eacd99-cbd2-5a9a-9dc8-341783ee145a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314324} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eecf3c03-86c6-5292-95c9-13caca188aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313881} {:answer/id #uuid "f7af75d5-0c09-5bcf-8ee2-db16821155a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7af75d5-0c09-5bcf-8ee2-db16821155a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313954} :answer-field/id #uuid "d18c9be6-d5aa-51a5-8758-1e88477bdd7a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fda84922-b86f-5e9f-ad04-1ae70c76ef22" :question/math-academy-id "q-339878" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-6y=6{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-3x},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{3x}$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{3x}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." :question/worked-solution "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{3x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{3x})^{′}=3{e}^{3x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(3{e}^{3x})^{′}=9{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(9{e}^{3x})+(3{e}^{3x})-6({e}^{3x})=6{e}^{3x}.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{3x}$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{3x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x{e}^{3x})^{′}={e}^{3x}+3x{e}^{3x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =({e}^{3x}+3x{e}^{3x})^{′}=6{e}^{3x}+9x{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(6{e}^{3x}+9x{e}^{3x})+({e}^{3x}+3x{e}^{3x})-6(x{e}^{3x})=6{e}^{3x}.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{3x}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-3x}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-3x}+{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c62ddfe-5b85-58c8-bd10-cfbeb2480fa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312068} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6e0781-126a-57fe-979e-48578b39a43a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312618} {:answer/id #uuid "91b7abd9-d77a-5419-90ef-b4a0e2a90f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313138} {:answer/id #uuid "a35e0c5b-17c5-5101-9ba9-544c94dc646d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Cx{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f6e0781-126a-57fe-979e-48578b39a43a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312618} :answer-field/id #uuid "1648b138-2746-531c-aa35-b21ab5dfe49e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59bd2ab0-