186313342} {:answer/id #uuid "be0627bc-ce71-59d6-b6c8-2b73727dbe76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313464} {:answer/id #uuid "dd61646a-7410-551c-baf8-7bbd779384ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be0627bc-ce71-59d6-b6c8-2b73727dbe76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313464} :answer-field/id #uuid "bca0208d-b9f4-582a-9ba5-1883456b8914" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314528} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43073a1f-2b5b-5703-a792-6e8555c72f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312510} {:answer/id #uuid "7e2c1c58-4d8a-5d33-8a55-4c1be51f27d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e2c1c58-4d8a-5d33-8a55-4c1be51f27d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312988} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb9e18e9-cc3d-5ba2-b3bf-d3bb65f2b186" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "58612e0b-7cd3-5b46-bfa2-b039e1e27a95" :question/math-academy-id "q-339879" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}-6y=-12{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-6x},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-2x}$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-2x}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." :question/worked-solution "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-2x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{-2x})^{′}=-2{e}^{-2x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(-2{e}^{-2x})^{′}=4{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(4{e}^{-2x})+5(-2{e}^{-2x})-6({e}^{-2x})=-12{e}^{-2x}.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-2x}$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-2x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x{e}^{-2x})^{′}={e}^{-2x}-2x{e}^{-2x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =({e}^{-2x}-2x{e}^{-2x})^{′}=-4{e}^{-2x}+4x{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(-4{e}^{-2x}+4x{e}^{-2x})+5({e}^{-2x}-2x{e}^{-2x})-6(x{e}^{-2x})=-12{e}^{-2x}.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-2x}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-6x}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-6x}+{e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cc96cd5-174b-5da6-a6fd-994e2dd4d267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Cx{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379530} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8b268a-19bf-5080-807b-9f597fcab82b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379531} {:answer/id #uuid "534c2f47-5692-5844-82b2-4cc0b8c2477a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379532} {:answer/id #uuid "56205c21-8b72-5fc2-bb90-375a54a8d523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "534c2f47-5692-5844-82b2-4cc0b8c2477a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379532} :answer-field/id #uuid "62fef4ab-b7ee-5741-8566-ebcd2ee1735d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee7c971b-eb0c-5fb8-991a-354e947be971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379535} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca8b6eb-5be4-5fa1-acac-a5574c7f727a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379536} {:answer/id #uuid "97283954-005a-5174-aa7a-cb81bae4d22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379537} {:answer/id #uuid "df